ms like Super  Mario Brothers and Street Fighter 2 more  recent and advised efforts such as  Assassin's Creed and Warcraft video game  movies are pretty much known for being  terrible but it's looking quite possible  that Detective Pikachu could break the  mold by becoming one of the first  live-action movies based off a video  game to earn widespread audience and  critical acclaim thanks to his  innovative CGI work audiences might  expect that Detective Pikachu was shot  with a heavy emphasis on motion capture  suits and green screen but as star just  a Smith told New York Magazine that  definitely wasn't the case according to  Smith the production made a point of  shooting on location as much as possible  using actual environments to help  enhance the reality of this live-action  Pokemon world filming took place in both  London and Scotland keeping green  screens to a minimum and using the  locations natural beauty and urban  backdrops to great effect director Rob  Letterman reportedly wanted to juxtapose  the fantastical world of Pokemon against  a gritty urban landscape to make the  creatures according to Smith pop more  also helping add the distinctive look of  the movie is the fact that it was shot  on film with the naturally grainy  quality helping to make the movie feel  like a realistic and gritty film noir  it's the source of small detail you  might not have noticed on its own  instead of viewers have just left with  the impression that the movie looks way  more realistic than they may have  expected in this  way another's detective Pikachu will  visibly set itself apart from any of us  animated predecessors in the Pokemon  series perhaps laying the track for a  whole new tradition for the franchise on  the big screen when the first trailer  for detective Pikachu dropped in  November 2018 audiences were both  confused and delighted compared to every  other Pokemon property it looked very  different but it also had a lot of charm  the first appearance of the title  character combining the cutesy look of  Pikachu with the quippy Ryan Reynolds  went over with viewers surprisingly well  before long a curious consensus started  growing  maybe the filmmakers has something here  the first trailer introduces a basic  story of Pikachu and Tim's quest to find  his missing father but it also made sure  viewers got glimpses of other Pokemon it  also made it clear that this Pikachu  would be a slightly more grown-up  iteration of the beloved children's  character getting adult fans who grew up  with a series more interested in the  movie than they might have expected they  would be the second trailer released in  February 2019  even more Pokemon alongside Pikachu  including the first glimpse of Muto the  menacing and hyper intelligent Pokemon  who headlined the series first animated  movie in 1998 the excitement and the  claim that Detective Pikachu's first  trailers kicked up has clearly been  encouraging to the people behind the  movie ahead of the film's release it's  already been announced that there's a  sequel in the works with a script being  written by Ori new zeal best known for  his writing credits on 22 Jump Street  the Cloverfield paradox and the upcoming  Sonic the Hedgehog whether or not the  director or start would return for a  sequel or what a sequel to the movie  would even be about it's still up in the  air but if detective Pikachu just well  enough with audiences at the box office  especially against the summer movie  juggernaut of Avengers endgame we  wouldn't be surprised if it kicked off a  whole new cinematic universe of  live-action Pokemon adventures for a  movie this off-the-wall and unexpected  that'd be a pretty shocking result check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite stuff are coming soon subscribe  to our YouTube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

